            <div id="pnlDepartmentInfo" class="col col-half">
	

                <h3 class="postingHeader">Department Information</h3>

                <div class="postingContent">
		
                    <p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">The California Department of Food and Agricultures Inspection Services Division, Center for Analytical Chemistry (CAC) provides valuable services to California related to food and environmental safety issues including crop protection, farm worker safety, data gathering activities, and emergency response. The CAC uses state of the art equipment and processes to test fruits, vegetables, nuts, and animal fertilizer, to ensure that pesticide and chemical levels are within the safety range established by national and international standards. The CAC also serves the nation as a member of the Food Emergency Response Network (FERN). CAC’s clients are comprised of local, state and federal governmental agencies that are responsible for monitoring the nation’s food supply.</span></p>
                
